PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Key disagreement remains A vs D (C/E now out). NI 45-106 (Jan 2021) unchanged: individuals via income ($200k/$300k spousal, 2 prior yrs + expectation), net financial assets ($1M), net assets ($5M); entities via own net assets ($5M on FS) or all owners AIs.

Prior belief intact: D fails—James+spouse=$285k < $300k threshold, no other individual test met for James, 1% share blocks “all owners AIs,” no corp FS net-assets figure given. A succeeds—3 LPs each meet individual financial/net-asset tests; GP holding co capitalized with $6M cash gifts (net assets >$5M, qualifies on entity test) so LP clears “all owners AIs” route.

Round-1 arguments: Pro-D (Colleagues 1,4,5,7,10,12) stress James defect + lack of entity test for D’s corp. Pro-A (Colleagues 2,3,6,8,9,11) claim GP capitalization/gifting insufficient to prove GP itself is AI or that ownership structure satisfies clause. No new facts alter thresholds or “all owners” wording; D’s 1% non-AI shareholder remains decisive flaw vs A’s entity-level qualification for GP. Unresolved: whether “gifted” language alone defeats A, but facts imply control + $6M cash satisfies bright-line test. Current belief unchanged: D is sole non-AI.}

